    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-281" contextRef="c-01">&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;None&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;None&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;None&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;None&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Company is organized a limited liability company and is treated as a flow-through entity for income tax purposes. As a result, the net taxable income or loss o the Company and any related tax credits, for income tax purposes, are deemed to pass to the Members of the Company even though such net taxable income for tax credits may have actually been distributed. Accordingly, no tax provision has been made in the financial statements of the Company since the income tax is an obligation of the Member.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;None&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
